{%- comment -%}
  Order canceled (docs/emails.md): why, in one clause, then what happens to the money, in the refund policy's terms
  (to the original payment method within 5 to 7 working days). Orders are prepaid or partial COD and are canceled
  before dispatch, so the only money paid is the online payment. It replaces Shopify's message, which said "staff
  error" and had no sentence for an order with nothing paid (kept as a safe fallback: "Nothing was charged").
{%- endcomment -%}
{% capture email_body %}
  {%- case cancel_reason -%}
    {%- when 'customer' -%}We've canceled order {{ name }} at your request.
    {%- when 'inventory' -%}We've had to cancel order {{ name }} because a piece you ordered is out of stock. We're sorry.
    {%- when 'declined' -%}Order {{ name }} was canceled because the payment didn't go through.
    {%- when 'staff' -%}We've canceled order {{ name }} because of a mistake on our side. We're sorry.
    {%- else -%}We've canceled order {{ name }}.
  {%- endcase %}
  {% if financial_status == 'refunded' or financial_status == 'partially_refunded' -%}
    Your refund is on its way to your original payment method and usually arrives in 5 to 7 working days.
  {%- elsif financial_status == 'voided' -%}
    The payment was released, so nothing was charged.
  {%- elsif financial_status == 'paid' or financial_status == 'partially_paid' -%}
    We'll refund what you paid to your original payment method within 5 to 7 working days.
  {%- elsif cancel_reason != 'declined' -%}
    Nothing was charged.
  {%- endif %}
{% endcapture %}
